# Auto-generated, perpetually-dirty manifests: never conflict on merge/rebase.
#
# books/<book>/translation-errors.json is regenerated by cnxml-inject on every
# run and is committed on both the dev box and the production server (the 2h
# git-backup cron stages it). That guarantees merge/rebase conflicts on every
# deploy pull. It is a derived artifact (rewritten on the next inject), so there
# is nothing to merge: keep the current side and move on.
#
# Requires the "ours" merge driver to be registered locally (it is NOT stored in
# the repo — git config lives in .git/config). One-time per clone:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# The production deploy script (scripts/deploy.sh) sets this before each pull.
#
# books/<book>/residue-report.<track>.json (the A2 EN-residue scan manifest) is
# the exact same class: cnxml-inject rewrites it on every run, so it is dirty on
# prod after each "Vista + Birta" and would otherwise wedge the deploy pull.
books/*/translation-errors.json merge=ours
books/*/residue-report.*.json merge=ours
